          "date": "2026-10-30 18:32:03.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: start conf-sanity MDTs in parallel",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: start conf-sanity MDTs in parallel\n\nconf-sanity starts its MDTs through its own start_mds(), one\nafter another, so the parallel mount added to setupall() does not\nreach it. The suite starts the MDTs around 250 times per run, and\nwith four MDTs each start costs about 6 seconds.\n\nStart MDT0000 first, then the others in parallel, as mountmds()\ndoes. PARALLEL_MOUNT=0 keeps the serial order.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: mdtcount=4 mdscount=2 testlist=conf-sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I708d6d1aa0f3df36f176f84f0f364b38b078e353\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
